  "transcript_segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 28.0,
      "text": "The lamps go thin, the console size, and all this shade."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.0,
      "end": 38.0,
      "text": "Behind my eyes."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.0,
      "end": 47.0,
      "text": "There are mornings with no handle, only carpet wall and weight."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.0,
      "end": 52.0,
      "text": "Every thought a lock is set, every limb loading gate."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.0,
      "end": 57.0,
      "text": "Then I find the hidden rail, and the drawer beside the bed."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.0,
      "end": 62.0,
      "text": "Small, bright, current, plain provision for the system in the red."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.0,
      "end": 68.0,
      "text": "No romance in the rescue, no cathedral, no parade."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.0,
      "end": 74.0,
      "text": "Just the backup voltage, humming, where the human battery free."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.0,
      "end": 81.0,
      "text": "Back up rail, hold the body, when the main line disappears."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.0,
      "end": 92.0,
      "text": "Bring the color to the panel, bring the floorboards back from Smith."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.0,
      "end": 102.0,
      "text": "I don't worship the small light, and I just need the room to stay."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.0,
      "end": 113.0,
      "text": "When the screen begins to turn, you return me to the day."
    },
    {
      "start": 114.0,
      "end": 121.0,
      "text": "People call it little comfort, as if comfort were a flaw."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.0,
      "end": 129.0,
      "text": "As if every fragile engine ought to run on night and all, but I know the sound of empty."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.0,
      "end": 137.0,
      "text": "When the meat is barely lit, I know how the whole apartment tilts around the missing gift."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.0,
      "end": 143.0,
      "text": "I keep a measured signal, not for pleasure, not for grace."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.0,
      "end": 150.0,
      "text": "Just the key, the old receiver from dissolving out of place."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.0,
      "end": 159.0,
      "text": "Dependent says an ugly word, until the rail goes cold."
    },
    {
      "start": 160.0,
      "end": 169.0,
      "text": "And every theory loses voltage, and the body tells the truth."
    },
